* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    call !acc_os_place(acc.name, staged.path, target.path, err)
*
* A per-OS helper of RESTORE.ACCOUNT (see !acc_archive).  target.path is the
* account's register path, and the account already exists - RESTORE.ACCOUNT
* has run create_account first when it had to.
*
* ON WINDOWS THE TARGET DIRECTORY STAYS AND ITS CONTENTS ARE SWAPPED.  Its
* explicit ACL is the account's grant (CREATE.ACCOUNT secure.account.dir); a
* directory moved into its place would carry the staging directory's ACL
* instead.  The old contents are moved aside first and removed only once all of
* the new ones are in; a failure before that puts everything back.  Then every
* child is reset to inherit the target's ACL, because a moved file keeps the
* one it had.  Both trees must hold a voc, so a wrong path cannot empty some
* other directory.  The work is sd-account-archive.ps1 -Mode Place.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine acc_os_place(acc.name, staged.path, target.path, err)
$catalog !acc_os_place

   counts = ''
   call !acc_archive('PLACE', '', staged.path : @fm : target.path, counts, err)
   return
end
